{"id":"diffeq","name":"Differential equations","cards":[{"id":"diffeq-1","sides":[{"text":"Order of an ODE","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"The order of the highest derivative present","sub":"","more":{"text":"y''+3y'=sin x is second-order.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-2","sides":[{"text":"Linear ODE","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"\\(a_n(x)y^{(n)}+\\dots+a_1(x)y'+a_0(x)y=g(x)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"y and its derivatives appear only to the first power and are not multiplied together.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-3","sides":[{"text":"General vs particular solution","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"General solution has n arbitrary constants; initial conditions pick the particular solution","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-4","sides":[{"text":"Initial value problem (IVP)","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"\\(y'=f(x,y),\\ y(x_0)=y_0\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-5","sides":[{"text":"Existence and uniqueness (Picard)","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"If f and ∂f/∂y are continuous near (x₀,y₀), a unique solution exists locally","sub":"","more":{"text":"y'=y^{2/3}, y(0)=0 has multiple solutions: ∂f/∂y blows up at 0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-6","sides":[{"text":"Direction field","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"Draw the slope f(x,y) at grid points; solutions follow the arrows","sub":"","more":{"text":"Isoclines: curves where the slope is constant.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-7","sides":[{"text":"Equilibrium solution","sub":"Beginner · Basics"},{"text":"y=c where f(c)=0 for autonomous y'=f(y)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Stable if nearby solutions approach it: f'(c)<0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-8","sides":[{"text":"Separable equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'=g(x)h(y)\\Rightarrow\\int\\frac{dy}{h(y)}=\\int g(x)\\,dx\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Check for lost constant solutions where h(y)=0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-9","sides":[{"text":"First-order linear","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'+P(x)y=Q(x),\\ \\mu=e^{\\int P\\,dx},\\ (\\mu y)'=\\mu Q\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Multiply by the integrating factor μ, then integrate.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-10","sides":[{"text":"Exact equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(M\\,dx+N\\,dy=0,\\ M_y=N_x\\Rightarrow F(x,y)=C\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Find F with F_x=M, F_y=N. If not exact, try an integrating factor that depends only on x or y.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-11","sides":[{"text":"Homogeneous (degree zero)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'=f(y/x):\\ v=y/x\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Gives a separable equation x v'=f(v)−v.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-12","sides":[{"text":"Bernoulli equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'+Py=Qy^n:\\ v=y^{1-n}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Becomes linear in v.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-13","sides":[{"text":"Riccati equation","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y'=q_0+q_1y+q_2y^2\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"If a particular solution y₁ is known, v=1/(y−y₁) makes it linear.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-14","sides":[{"text":"Substitution v = ax + by + c","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"For y'=f(ax+by+c), set v=ax+by+c to separate","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-15","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y'=x y\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} e^{\\frac{x^{2}}{2}}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-16","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y'=y^{2}\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y=- \\frac{1}{C_{1} + x}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-17","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(2 y + y'=e^{- x}\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} e^{- 2 x} + e^{- x}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-18","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(x y' + y=x^{2}\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y=\\frac{C_{1}}{x} + \\frac{x^{2}}{3}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-19","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(- y + y'=x,\\ y(0)=1\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y=- x + 2 e^{x} - 1\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-20","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y'=\\frac{x^{2} + 1}{y},\\ y(0)=2\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y=\\frac{\\sqrt{6 x^{3} + 18 x + 36}}{3}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-21","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y' + \\frac{y}{x}=y^{2}\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(y=\\frac{1}{C_{1} x - x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-22","sides":[{"text":"Exact: \\((2xy+1)dx+(x^2+3y^2)dy=0\\)","sub":"Beginner · First-order methods"},{"text":"\\(x^2y+x+y^3=C\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"M_y=2x=N_x. F=∫M dx = x²y+x+g(y); F_y=x²+g'=x²+3y² ⇒ g=y³.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-23","sides":[{"text":"Exponential growth/decay","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{dP}{dt}=kP\\Rightarrow P=P_0e^{kt}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Half-life T: k=−ln2/T. Doubling time ln2/k.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-24","sides":[{"text":"Newton's law of cooling","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(T'=-k(T-T_{env})\\Rightarrow T=T_{env}+(T_0-T_{env})e^{-kt}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-25","sides":[{"text":"Mixing tank","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{dA}{dt}=r_{in}c_{in}-r_{out}\\frac{A}{V(t)}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Rate in minus rate out; V(t) changes if flows differ.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-26","sides":[{"text":"Logistic equation","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(P'=rP\\left(1-\\frac PK\\right),\\ P=\\frac K{1+Ae^{-rt}}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Equilibria 0 (unstable) and K (stable). Fastest growth at P=K/2.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-27","sides":[{"text":"Terminal velocity (linear drag)","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(mv'=mg-kv\\Rightarrow v_\\infty=mg/k\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-28","sides":[{"text":"Series RL circuit","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"\\(L i'+Ri=E\\Rightarrow i=\\frac ER(1-e^{-Rt/L})\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Time constant L/R.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-29","sides":[{"text":"Orthogonal trajectories","sub":"Beginner · Models"},{"text":"Replace dy/dx by −dx/dy in the family's ODE and solve","sub":"","more":{"text":"Orthogonal to y=cx² is x²+2y²=k.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-30","sides":[{"text":"Euler's method","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods"},{"text":"\\(y_{n+1}=y_n+hf(x_n,y_n)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Global error O(h).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-31","sides":[{"text":"Improved Euler (Heun)","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods"},{"text":"\\(y_{n+1}=y_n+\\tfrac h2[f_n+f(x_{n+1},y_n+hf_n)]\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Global error O(h²).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-32","sides":[{"text":"Runge–Kutta 4","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods"},{"text":"\\(y_{n+1}=y_n+\\tfrac h6(k_1+2k_2+2k_3+k_4)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Global error O(h⁴). Workhorse of numerical ODE solving.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-33","sides":[{"text":"Euler, h=0.1, for y'=x+y, y(0)=1: find y(0.2)","sub":"Beginner · Numerical methods"},{"text":"1.220","sub":"","more":{"text":"y₁=1+0.1(0+1)=1.1; y₂=1.1+0.1(0.1+1.1)=1.22.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-34","sides":[{"text":"Characteristic equation","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(ay''+by'+cy=0\\to ar^2+br+c=0\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-35","sides":[{"text":"Distinct real roots","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=c_1e^{r_1x}+c_2e^{r_2x}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-36","sides":[{"text":"Repeated root","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=(c_1+c_2x)e^{rx}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-37","sides":[{"text":"Complex roots \\(\\alpha\\pm\\beta i\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=e^{\\alpha x}(c_1\\cos\\beta x+c_2\\sin\\beta x)\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-38","sides":[{"text":"Superposition and general solution","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Solutions of a homogeneous linear ODE form a vector space of dimension n","sub":"","more":{"text":"General nonhomogeneous solution = y_h + y_p.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-39","sides":[{"text":"Wronskian","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(W=\\begin{vmatrix}y_1&y_2\\\\y_1'&y_2'\\end{vmatrix}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Nonzero on an interval ⇒ y₁, y₂ linearly independent.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-40","sides":[{"text":"Reduction of order","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Given y₁, set y₂=v(x)y₁ and the equation becomes first-order in v'","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-41","sides":[{"text":"Method of undetermined coefficients","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Guess y_p from the forcing term; multiply by x (or x²) if it duplicates a homogeneous solution","sub":"","more":{"text":"e^{kx}→Ae^{kx}; sin/cos→A cos+B sin; polynomial degree n→ full degree n polynomial.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-42","sides":[{"text":"Variation of parameters","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y_p=-y_1\\int\\frac{y_2g}W+y_2\\int\\frac{y_1g}W\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"For y''+py'+qy=g with leading coefficient 1. Works for any g.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-43","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(6 y - 5 y' + y''=0\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} e^{2 x} + C_{2} e^{3 x}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-44","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(4 y + y''=0\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + C_{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-45","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y + 2 y' + y''=0\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} e^{- x} + C_{2} x e^{- x}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-46","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(- y + y''=0,\\ y(0)=0,\\ y'(0)=1\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=\\frac{e^{x}}{2} - \\frac{e^{- x}}{2}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-47","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y + y''=0,\\ y(0)=1,\\ y'(0)=0\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-48","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(5 y + 2 y' + y''=0\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} e^{- x} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + C_{2} e^{- x} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-49","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(2 y - 3 y' + y''=e^{3 x}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} e^{x} + C_{2} e^{2 x} + \\frac{e^{3 x}}{2}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-50","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y + y''=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + C_{2} \\cos{\\left(x \\right)} + \\frac{x \\sin{\\left(x \\right)}}{2}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-51","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(4 y + y''=x^{2}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} \\sin{\\left(2 x \\right)} + C_{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x \\right)} + \\frac{x^{2}}{4} - \\frac{1}{8}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-52","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y - 2 y' + y''=e^{x}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=C_{1} e^{x} + C_{2} x e^{x} + \\frac{x^{2} e^{x}}{2}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-53","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(y''+y=\\tan x\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"\\(y=c_1\\cos x+c_2\\sin x-\\cos x\\,\\ln|\\sec x+\\tan x|\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Variation of parameters: W=1, y_p=−cos x∫tan x sin x dx + sin x∫sin x dx.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-54","sides":[{"text":"Resonance","sub":"Intermediate · Second-order linear (constant coefficients)"},{"text":"Forcing frequency equals natural frequency: y_p contains t·sin(ωt), amplitude grows without bound","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-55","sides":[{"text":"Spring-mass equation","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(my''+cy'+ky=F(t)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"ω₀=√(k/m) natural frequency, c damping.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-56","sides":[{"text":"Damping regimes","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(c^2-4mk:\\ >0\\text{ overdamped},\\ =0\\text{ critical},\\ <0\\text{ underdamped}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Only underdamped oscillates, with decaying envelope e^{−ct/2m}.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-57","sides":[{"text":"Beats","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"Forcing near natural frequency: amplitude waxes and wanes at the difference frequency","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-58","sides":[{"text":"Series RLC circuit","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(Lq''+Rq'+q/C=E(t)\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Mathematically identical to the spring-mass system.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-59","sides":[{"text":"Cauchy–Euler equation","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(x^2y''+axy'+by=0:\\ y=x^r\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Indicial equation r(r−1)+ar+b=0; repeated root gives x^r ln x. Or let x=e^t.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-60","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(x^{2} y'' - 2 y=0\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"\\(y=\\frac{C_{1}}{x} + C_{2} x^{2}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-61","sides":[{"text":"Higher-order constant-coefficient","sub":"Intermediate · Vibrations and Euler equations"},{"text":"Roots of the degree-n characteristic polynomial; multiplicity m gives x^k e^{rx}, k<m","sub":"","more":{"text":"y'''−y=0: roots 1, e^{±2πi/3}.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-62","sides":[{"text":"Definition","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{f\\}=\\int_0^\\infty e^{-st}f(t)\\,dt\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-63","sides":[{