tiplication by t","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{tf\\}=-F'(s)\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-76","sides":[{"text":"Unit step and second shift","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{u(t-a)f(t-a)\\}=e^{-as}F(s)\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-77","sides":[{"text":"Dirac delta","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{\\delta(t-a)\\}=e^{-as}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Models an instantaneous impulse; the delta is the derivative of the step.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-78","sides":[{"text":"Convolution theorem","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{f*g\\}=F(s)G(s),\\ (f*g)(t)=\\int_0^tf(\\tau)g(t-\\tau)d\\tau\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-79","sides":[{"text":"Periodic functions","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\mathcal L\\{f\\}=\\frac1{1-e^{-sT}}\\int_0^Te^{-st}f\\,dt\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-80","sides":[{"text":"Laplace method recipe","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"Transform the ODE ⇒ solve algebraically for Y(s) ⇒ partial fractions ⇒ invert","sub":"","more":{"text":"Initial conditions are built in.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-81","sides":[{"text":"Inverse transform of \\(\\frac{1}{s \\left(s + 1\\right)}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(1 - e^{- t}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-82","sides":[{"text":"Inverse transform of \\(\\frac{1}{s^{2} + 4 s + 13}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\frac{e^{- 2 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}}{3}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-83","sides":[{"text":"Inverse transform of \\(\\frac{s}{\\left(s + 1\\right) \\left(s + 2\\right)}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(\\left(2 - e^{t}\\right) e^{- 2 t}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-84","sides":[{"text":"Inverse transform of \\(\\frac{1}{s^{2} \\left(s^{2} + 1\\right)}\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(t - \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-85","sides":[{"text":"Solve with Laplace: \\(y''+y=\\sin 2t,\\ y(0)=y'(0)=0\\)","sub":"Intermediate · Laplace transforms"},{"text":"\\(y=\\)\\(\\frac{2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}{3} - \\frac{\\sin{\\left(2 t \\right)}}{3}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"(s²+1)Y=2/(s²+4) ⇒ Y=2/((s²+1)(s²+4)).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-86","sides":[{"text":"Linear system","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x'=A\\mathbf x\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Solutions e^{λt}v where Av=λv.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-87","sides":[{"text":"Distinct real eigenvalues","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x=c_1e^{\\lambda_1t}\\mathbf v_1+c_2e^{\\lambda_2t}\\mathbf v_2\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Same sign: node. Opposite sign: saddle.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-88","sides":[{"text":"Complex eigenvalues \\(\\alpha\\pm i\\beta\\)","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"Spiral (α≠0): sink if α<0, source if α>0; center if α=0","sub":"","more":{"text":"Real solutions from real and imaginary parts of e^{λt}v.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-89","sides":[{"text":"Repeated eigenvalue","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"Defective: x = c₁e^{λt}v + c₂e^{λt}(tv+w) with (A−λI)w=v","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-90","sides":[{"text":"Trace–determinant classification","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"Det<0 saddle; det>0 and tr²>4det node; tr²<4det spiral; tr<0 stable; tr>0 unstable","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-91","sides":[{"text":"Fundamental matrix","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x=e^{At}\\mathbf x_0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Matrix exponential; compute with diagonalization or Jordan form.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-92","sides":[{"text":"Nonhomogeneous systems","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x_p=\\Phi\\int\\Phi^{-1}\\mathbf g\\,dt\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Variation of parameters for systems.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-93","sides":[{"text":"Eigenvalues of \\(\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 2\\\\3 & 2\\end{matrix}\\right]\\) for the system x′=Ax","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(-1\\), \\(4\\) ⇒ saddle (opposite signs)","sub":"","more":{"text":"λ²−3λ−4=(λ−4)(λ+1).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-94","sides":[{"text":"Solve \\(x'=x+2y,\\ y'=3x+2y\\)","sub":"Advanced · Systems"},{"text":"\\(\\mathbf x=c_1e^{4t}\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}+c_2e^{-t}\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}\\)","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-95","sides":[{"text":"Phase plane","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"Plot trajectories of (x',y')=(f,g) in the x–y plane; equilibria where f=g=0","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-96","sides":[{"text":"Linearization at an equilibrium","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"\\(J=\\begin{pmatrix}f_x&f_y\\\\g_x&g_y\\end{pmatrix}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Eigenvalues of the Jacobian classify the equilibrium (Hartman–Grobman), except borderline centers.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-97","sides":[{"text":"Lotka–Volterra predator–prey","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"\\(x'=ax-bxy,\\ y'=-cy+dxy\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Closed orbits around (c/d, a/b); a conserved quantity exists.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-98","sides":[{"text":"Lyapunov function","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"V positive definite with V' ≤ 0 along trajectories ⇒ stable; V'<0 ⇒ asymptotically stable","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-99","sides":[{"text":"Limit cycle","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"An isolated closed orbit; e.g. van der Pol oscillator","sub":"","more":{"text":"Poincaré–Bendixson: bounded trajectory with no equilibria in the plane approaches a closed orbit.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-100","sides":[{"text":"Bifurcation","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"A qualitative change in the equilibria as a parameter varies","sub":"","more":{"text":"Saddle-node, transcritical, pitchfork, Hopf.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-101","sides":[{"text":"Chaos","sub":"Advanced · Nonlinear and qualitative"},{"text":"Sensitive dependence on initial conditions; needs at least 3 dimensions for continuous systems","sub":"","more":{"text":"Lorenz system is the standard example.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-102","sides":[{"text":"Power series solution","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(y=\\sum a_nx^n\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Plug in, shift indices, match powers to get a recurrence for a_n. Works near ordinary points.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-103","sides":[{"text":"Ordinary vs singular point","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"x₀ is ordinary if the equation in standard form y''+py'+qy=0 has analytic p and q there","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-104","sides":[{"text":"Frobenius method","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(y=x^r\\sum a_nx^n\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Regular singular point; indicial equation determines r; the second solution may include ln x.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-105","sides":[{"text":"Bessel's equation","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(x^2y''+xy'+(x^2-\\nu^2)y=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Solutions J_ν and Y_ν; appears in circular drums.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-106","sides":[{"text":"Legendre's equation","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\((1-x^2)y''-2xy'+n(n+1)y=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Polynomial solutions P_n; spherical problems.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-107","sides":[{"text":"Airy equation","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\(y''-xy=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Power series solution; oscillates for x<0, decays for x>0.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-108","sides":[{"text":"Sturm–Liouville problem","sub":"Advanced · Series solutions and special equations"},{"text":"\\((py')'+(q+\\lambda w)y=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Eigenvalues real; eigenfunctions orthogonal with weight w.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-109","sides":[{"text":"Fourier series","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(f=\\frac{a_0}2+\\sum a_n\\cos\\frac{n\\pi x}L+b_n\\sin\\frac{n\\pi x}L\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"a_n=(1/L)∫f cos, b_n=(1/L)∫f sin over [−L,L].","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-110","sides":[{"text":"Even/odd shortcuts","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"Even f: only cosines. Odd f: only sines","sub":"","more":{"text":"Half-range expansions extend f evenly or oddly.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-111","sides":[{"text":"Parseval / Dirichlet","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"The series converges to the midpoint of jump discontinuities","sub":""}]},{"id":"diffeq-112","sides":[{"text":"Heat equation","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(u_t=\\alpha u_{xx}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Separation of variables: u=X(x)T(t). With u=0 at ends of [0,L]: Σ b_n e^{-α(nπ/L)²t} sin(nπx/L).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-113","sides":[{"text":"Wave equation","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(u_{tt}=c^2u_{xx}\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"d'Alembert: u=F(x−ct)+G(x+ct).","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-114","sides":[{"text":"Laplace's equation","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"\\(u_{xx}+u_{yy}=0\\)","sub":"","more":{"text":"Harmonic functions; maximum principle.","sub":""}}]},{"id":"diffeq-115","sides":[{"text":"Separation of variables recipe","sub":"Advanced · Fourier series and PDEs"},{"text":"Assume u=X·T, split into two ODEs with separation constant −λ, solve the eigenvalue problem, superpose, fit initial data with Fourier series","sub":""}]}]}